Package: aTPRAIPW
Title: Adjusted True Positive Rates with Partially Observed Outcomes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ruofan", "Wang", email = "ruofanwa@upenn.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Estimates risk-standardized true positive rate differences
    between two subgroups when gold-standard outcomes are available for
    known noncases and a selectively validated subset of candidates.
    Extends 'fairRisk' with covariate-based and phenotype-assisted augmented
    inverse probability weighting and stacked influence-function standard
    errors. Uses 'fairRisk' for ordinary logistic calibration, linear and
    quadratic logit density-ratio models, and adjusted true positive rate
    aggregation. Includes complete-case, contaminated-label, and
    full-data comparisons. Synthetic simulation examples are provided in
    the source repository separately from the estimation functions.
